    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d146">

                <pb facs="0345" n="221" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg221"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">175.1/41: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Vice Consul at Jerusalem</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Cobb</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Jerusalem</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-07-20T16:00:00+02:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 20, 1923—4
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received July 21—4:55
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Reference capitulations: Chief Justice Palestine Government has verbally informed
                    me that our capitulations are not in accord with the Palestine order in council
                    (enclosure to my despatch no. 1018, September 6, 1922<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d146-f1"/>) and Attorney General has verbally informed me local
                    government cannot force him to comply with instructions of the Chief Secretary,
                    referred to in my despatch no. 1104, March 3, 1923, though lower courts have and
                    are continuing to do so. <pb facs="0346" n="222" xml:id="pg222"/> Article 87 of
                    the aforementioned order in council authorizes High Commissioner to amend order
                    in council but for political reasons it appears inexpedient to local government
                    lest other nations who have not successfully maintained their capitulations
                    might be offended. It appears necessary that action to this end be taken through
                    London.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cobb</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
